<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 10: </span>Top words in the <span id="A3.T10.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">text of the generated story by Mixtral model</span> that correlate (Pearson) with the sociocultural factor. The terms <span id="A3.T10.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">child</span>, <span id="A3.T10.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">daughter</span>, and <span id="A3.T10.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">son</span> have been removed, as they are almost present at the start of the generation</figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Protagonist Analysis</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A3.T11" title="In C.1 Protagonist Analysis ‣ Appendix C Story Analysis ‣ Biased Tales: Cultural and Topic Bias in Generating Children’s Stories" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> shows the top words in children attributes in the generated story that correlate (Pearson) with the target sociocultural variable (e.g., child gender or parent’s nationality).</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T11" class="ltx_table">
