<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Diversity Analysis</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A3.T15" title="In C.2 Diversity Analysis ‣ Appendix C Story Analysis ‣ Biased Tales: Cultural and Topic Bias in Generating Children’s Stories" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a> shows Average inner product similarity with all-MiniLM-L6-v2, between stories generated with specific prompts. A lower number means higher diversity, which is better. In addition, we observe average inner product similarity across different models in <a href="#A3.T16" title="In C.2 Diversity Analysis ‣ Appendix C Story Analysis ‣ Biased Tales: Cultural and Topic Bias in Generating Children’s Stories" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>, <a href="#A3.T17" title="In C.2 Diversity Analysis ‣ Appendix C Story Analysis ‣ Biased Tales: Cultural and Topic Bias in Generating Children’s Stories" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>, and <a href="#A3.T18" title="In C.2 Diversity Analysis ‣ Appendix C Story Analysis ‣ Biased Tales: Cultural and Topic Bias in Generating Children’s Stories" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>.</p>
</div>
